WEBVTT
NOTE AIR website demo — captions timed to a 75-second cut; retime after recording.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.500
This is a real drone crash — a public flight log anyone can download.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:14.000
The owner's entire analysis was one sentence: "my drone started to gain altitude sharply."

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Drop that log into AIR. Under a second later, it's an incident record.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Seven findings, each typed: measured evidence, the threshold it tripped, and where that threshold comes from.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.500
Battery hit zero percent — while it was still flying.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:44.000
AIR checked the flight against written procedures. Altitude limit 120 meters: the flight hit 120.04.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Two independent altitude sensors disagree by twenty meters at the crash. AIR reports the conflict — it doesn't pick a winner.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:02.000
And the whole record is sealed: hash tree, signature, offline verifier. Change one byte, verification fails.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.500
It's early: PX4 logs only, a 100-log public evaluation, every limitation published.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:15.000
If you investigate real incidents, bring one log and twenty minutes. air.findanything.dev
